    "q-82626": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82626",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the converse of the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ **If** you can play in the garden, **then** it is not raining.",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ You can play in the garden.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ It is not raining.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is not raining, then you can play in the garden.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
