    "q-183292": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183292",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the converse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** $\\pi \\in Z,$ **then** $7$ is composite.",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ $\\pi \\in Z.$\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $7$ is composite.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $7$ is composite, then $\\pi \\in Z.$",
