    "q-183294": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183294",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the converse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** there are no clouds in the sky, **then** it is not raining.",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ There are no clouds in the sky.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ It is not raining.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is not raining, then there are no clouds in the sky.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
