    "q-81982": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81982",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** my pet is not a fish, **then** it needs a food bowl.",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ My pet is not a fish.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ It needs a food bowl.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ My pet is a fish.\n\n- $¬B:$ It does not need a food bowl.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If my pet is a fish, then it does not need a food bowl.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
