    "q-171332": {
      "dom_id": "step-q171332",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Find the contrapositive of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** $\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{2,3\\}=∅,$ **then** $6$ is prime.",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ $\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{2,3\\}=∅.$\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $6$ is prime.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ $\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{2,3\\}\\ne ∅.$\n\n- $¬B:$ $6$ is not prime.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $6$ is not prime, then $\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{2,3\\}\\ne ∅.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-171332-a",
