    "q-106796": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106796",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Find the contrapositive of the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ **If** it does not get warmer, **then** the sun does not come out.",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It does not get warmer.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ The sun does not come out.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It gets warmer.\n\n- $¬B:$ The sun comes out.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If the sun comes out, then it gets warm.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
