    "q-183338": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183338",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Find the contrapositive of the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ **If** Mary isn't late for work, **then** the boss isn't upset.",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ Mary isn't late for work.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$  The boss isn't upset.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ Mary is late for work.\n\n- $¬B:$ The boss is upset.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If the boss is upset, then Mary is late for work.",
